The debug info of inline functions, member functions and templates, the COMDAT
.debug$S sections that every object emitting the function repeats, moves to
the pack: each object keeps a 24-byte reference and the section's relocations.
Packed objects materialize back to their exact bytes, and links of the packed
objects are byte-identical to links of the originals.

The inputs were compiled with
  clang-cl /c /Z7 -gcodeview-ghash /Od /GS- /Zl /GR- /Brepro
from these sources (fn.h, a.cpp, b.cpp):

  // fn.h
  struct Counter { int n; int bump(int by) { n += by; return n; } };
  inline int twice(int x) { int y = x * 2; return y; }
  template <typename T> T pick(T a, T b) { return a < b ? b : a; }
  // a.cpp
  #include "fn.h"
  int fa(Counter &c, int x) { return c.bump(twice(x)) + pick(x, 3); }
  // b.cpp
  #include "fn.h"
  int fb(Counter *c, int x) { return pick(c->bump(x), twice(x)); }

RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/orig %t/work
RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/cvpacks-fn-a.yaml -o %t/orig/a.obj
RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/cvpacks-fn-b.yaml -o %t/orig/b.obj

Counter::bump, twice and pick<int> are in both objects: six sections, three
pack functions.
RUN: llvm-cvpack pack --pack-path=%t/packs \
RUN:   --out-dir=%t/stage %t/orig/a.obj %t/orig/b.obj

RUN: llvm-readobj --sections %t/stage/a.obj | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STUB
RUN: llvm-readobj --sections %t/stage/b.obj | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STUB
STUB-COUNT-3: RawDataSize: 0x18{{$}}
STUB-NOT:     RawDataSize: 0x18{{$}}

RUN: %python -c "import json,shutil; p=json.load(open(r'%t/stage/cvpacks.json'))['packs'][0]; shutil.copyfile(r'%t/packs/' + p + '.cvp', r'%t/pack.cvp')"
RUN: llvm-cvpack dump %t/pack.cvp | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DUMP
DUMP:      Types:
DUMP-NEXT: Symbols:
DUMP-NEXT: Files: 1
DUMP-NEXT: Functions: 3

Packed objects materialize back to their original bytes.
RUN: llvm-cvpack materialize --pack-path=%t/packs %t/stage/a.obj -o %t/a.restored.obj
RUN: llvm-cvpack materialize --pack-path=%t/packs %t/stage/b.obj -o %t/b.restored.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/orig/a.obj %t/a.restored.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/orig/b.obj %t/b.restored.obj

Links of the packed objects, with and without global type hashing, are
byte-identical to links of the originals. The packs are in a directory of their
own, which the links search as they search for a library.
RUN: %python -c "import shutil; [shutil.copyfile(r'%t/orig/' + f, r'%t/work/' + f) for f in ('a.obj', 'b.obj')]"
RUN: lld-link /noentry /dll /nodefaultlib /debug /timestamp:0 /pdbaltpath:fn.pdb \
RUN:   /libpath:%t/packs /pdb:%t/work/out.pdb /out:%t/work/out.dll %t/work/a.obj %t/work/b.obj
RUN: %python -c "import shutil; shutil.copyfile(r'%t/work/out.pdb', r'%t/orig.pdb'); shutil.copyfile(r'%t/work/out.dll', r'%t/orig.dll')"
RUN: lld-link /noentry /dll /nodefaultlib /debug:noghash /timestamp:0 /pdbaltpath:fn.pdb \
RUN:   /libpath:%t/packs /pdb:%t/work/out.pdb /out:%t/work/out.dll %t/work/a.obj %t/work/b.obj
RUN: %python -c "import shutil; shutil.copyfile(r'%t/work/out.pdb', r'%t/orig-noghash.pdb')"
RUN: %python -c "import shutil; [shutil.copyfile(r'%t/stage/' + f, r'%t/work/' + f) for f in ('a.obj', 'b.obj')]"
RUN: lld-link /noentry /dll /nodefaultlib /debug /timestamp:0 /pdbaltpath:fn.pdb \
RUN:   /libpath:%t/packs /pdb:%t/work/out.pdb /out:%t/work/out.dll %t/work/a.obj %t/work/b.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/orig.pdb %t/work/out.pdb
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/orig.dll %t/work/out.dll
RUN: lld-link /noentry /dll /nodefaultlib /debug:noghash /timestamp:0 /pdbaltpath:fn.pdb \
RUN:   /libpath:%t/packs /pdb:%t/work/out.pdb /out:%t/work/out.dll %t/work/a.obj %t/work/b.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/orig-noghash.pdb %t/work/out.pdb

Packing the originals again against the dedup set reuses the pack, function
debug info included, and stages the same objects.
RUN: llvm-cvpack pack --pack-path=%t/packs \
RUN:   --out-dir=%t/stage2 %t/orig/a.obj %t/orig/b.obj
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REUSE < %t/stage2/cvpacks.json
REUSE-NOT: "packs": []
REUSE:     "new_packs": [],
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/stage/a.obj %t/stage2/a.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/stage/b.obj %t/stage2/b.obj
